IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `types`
IMPORT `chapter-4-exceptions`
IMPORT `chapter-4a-private-defence`

§ `Chapter 16 -- Causing miscarriage; injuries to unborn children; exposure of infants; and concealment of births`

-- Penal Code 1871 ss 312, 313, 314, 315, 316, 317, 318.
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt.
--
-- The Act's own sub-heading names four subjects, and the group is small but not
-- uniform: ss 312 to 316 are about the pregnancy and the unborn or newly born child,
-- s 317 about abandoning a living child, s 318 about concealing a birth by disposing
-- of a dead body.
--
-- ss 312, 314 and 315 each open "Subject to the provisions of the Termination of
-- Pregnancy Act 1974". That Act is not in this source bundle, so whether the act
-- falls within it is a caller-asserted fact, and it is encoded as a negated conjunct
-- on each of those three sections -- which is what "subject to" does. It is the same
-- treatment given to the Electronic Transactions Act 2010 in s 29B and to the
-- Organised Crime Act 2015 in s 308A: the cross-referenced Act's own test is not
-- re-derived here.
--
-- This group is also where s 299 Explanation 3 points. That Explanation takes the
-- child in the womb out of homicide; ss 312 to 316 are the sections that deal with
-- it instead.

§§ `Sections 312 and 313 -- Causing miscarriage`

-- s 312: whoever voluntarily causes a woman with child to miscarry. Its Explanation
-- brings the woman who causes herself to miscarry within the section, so that is a
-- second route to the conduct and not a separate offence.
-- The greater punishment where the pregnancy is of more than 16 weeks' duration is
-- punishment only; the fact is carried so a caller can see it.
-- s 313: the same offence committed without the woman's consent, "whether the
-- woman's pregnancy is of more than 16 weeks' duration or not" -- so the duration
-- fact is expressly immaterial to s 313 and is not conjoined with it.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 312"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes causing miscarriage under Penal Code 1871 section 312
GIVEN u IS AN `Unborn And Infants` @desc Voluntarily causing a woman with child to miscarry, or a woman causing herself to miscarry, where the act is not within the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes causing miscarriage` IF
        (   u's `voluntarily causes a woman with child to miscarry`
         OR u's `the woman causes herself to miscarry`)
    AND (NOT u's `the act is within the provisions of the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974`)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 313"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes causing miscarriage without the woman's consent under Penal Code 1871 section 313
GIVEN u IS AN `Unborn And Infants` @desc The s 312 offence, committed without the consent of the woman. The duration of the pregnancy is immaterial to this section.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes causing miscarriage without consent` IF
        `constitutes causing miscarriage` u
    AND u's `without the consent of the woman`

§§ `Section 314 -- Death caused by an act done with intent to cause miscarriage`

-- Whoever, with intent to cause the miscarriage of a woman with child, does any act
-- which causes the death of that woman.
-- The Explanation states that it is not essential that the offender should know the
-- act is likely to cause death. That removes a fault element rather than adding one,
-- so nothing is conjoined for it: the section is complete on the intent to cause
-- miscarriage plus the death.
-- The heavier punishment where the act is done without the woman's consent is
-- punishment only; the consent fact is already carried for s 313.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 314"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes causing death by an act done with intent to cause miscarriage under Penal Code 1871 section 314
GIVEN u IS AN `Unborn And Infants` @desc An act done with intent to cause the miscarriage of a woman with child, which causes her death. Knowledge that death was likely is not required.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes causing death with intent to cause miscarriage` IF
        u's `with intent to cause the miscarriage of a woman with child does an act which causes the death of that woman`
    AND (NOT u's `the act is within the provisions of the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974`)

§§ `Section 315 -- Child destruction before, at or immediately after birth`

-- s 315(1): whoever, with intent to destroy the life of a child capable of being born
-- alive, by any intentional act causes a child to die before it has an existence
-- independent of its mother, or by such act causes the child to die after its birth,
-- unless such act is immediately necessary to save the life of the mother.
--
-- The saving for the mother's life is written into the section, so it is a negated
-- conjunct here rather than something the wrapper applies.
-- s 315(2) makes pregnancy of 28 weeks or more prima facie evidence that the woman
-- was pregnant of a child capable of being born alive. That is a rule of evidence,
-- not an element: it tells a court what may be presumed, not what must be proved. The
-- fact is carried so a caller can assert it, and it is not conjoined.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 315(1)"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes child destruction under Penal Code 1871 section 315
GIVEN u IS AN `Unborn And Infants` @desc An intentional act done with intent to destroy the life of a child capable of being born alive, causing it to die before it has an independent existence or after its birth, and not immediately necessary to save the mother's life.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes child destruction` IF
        u's `with intent to destroy the life of a child capable of being born alive`
    AND (   u's `by an intentional act causes a child to die before it has an existence independent of its mother`
         OR u's `by such act causes the child to die after its birth`)
    AND (NOT u's `the act was immediately necessary to save the life of the mother`)
    AND (NOT u's `the act is within the provisions of the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974`)

§§ `Section 316 -- Causing the death of a quick unborn child`

-- Whoever does any act under such circumstances that if he thereby caused death he
-- would be guilty of culpable homicide, and does by such act cause the death of a
-- quick unborn child.
-- The Illustration is the case the section is for: an act likely to kill a pregnant
-- woman, which injures her without killing her but kills the quick unborn child.
-- The culpable-homicide circumstance is a counterfactual about the offender's state
-- of mind, so it is carried as its own fact rather than computed from the Homicide
-- record -- no death of a person has occurred to test s 299 against.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 316"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes causing the death of a quick unborn child under Penal Code 1871 section 316
GIVEN u IS AN `Unborn And Infants` @desc An act done in circumstances that would be culpable homicide had it caused death, which causes the death of a quick unborn child.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes causing the death of a quick unborn child` IF
        u's `does an act under such circumstances that if he thereby caused death he would be guilty of culpable homicide`
    AND u's `by such act causes the death of a quick unborn child`

§§ `Section 317 -- Exposure and abandonment of a child below 12`

-- Whoever, being the father or mother of a child below 12 years of age, or having
-- the care of such child, exposes or leaves such child in any place with the
-- intention of wholly abandoning it.
-- The Explanation preserves a trial for murder or culpable homicide if the child
-- dies in consequence of the exposure. That is a rule about what else may be
-- charged, not a condition of s 317, and adds no limb.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 317"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes exposure and abandonment of a child under Penal Code 1871 section 317
GIVEN u IS AN `Unborn And Infants` @desc A parent or person having care of a child below 12 who exposes or leaves the child anywhere, intending wholly to abandon it.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes exposure and abandonment of a child` IF
        u's `being the father or mother of a child below 12 years of age or having the care of such child`
    AND u's `exposes or leaves such child in any place`
    AND u's `with the intention of wholly abandoning such child`

§§ `Section 318 -- Concealment of a birth by secret disposal of the dead body`

-- Whoever, by secretly burying or otherwise disposing of the dead body of a child --
-- whether the child died before, after or during its birth -- intentionally conceals
-- or endeavours to conceal the birth of that child.
-- Note "or endeavours to conceal": the offence is complete on the attempt, so no
-- separate s 511 analysis is needed for the concealment.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 318"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes concealment of a birth by secret disposal of a dead body under Penal Code 1871 section 318
GIVEN u IS AN `Unborn And Infants` @desc Secretly burying or otherwise disposing of the dead body of a child, intending to conceal or endeavouring to conceal the birth.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes concealment of a birth` IF
        u's `by secretly burying or otherwise disposing of the dead body of a child`
    AND u's `intentionally conceals or endeavours to conceal the birth of such child`

§§ `Proposed Act wrappers`

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes causing miscarriage` IF
        `constitutes causing miscarriage` (a's `unborn and infants`)
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes child destruction` IF
        `constitutes child destruction` (a's `unborn and infants`)
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes exposure or abandonment of a child` IF
        `constitutes exposure and abandonment of a child` (a's `unborn and infants`)
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes concealment of a birth` IF
        `constitutes concealment of a birth` (a's `unborn and infants`)
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)
